<title>GREECE: GREEK PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) RAISES GASOLINE PRICES.</title>
<headline>GREEK PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) RAISES GASOLINE PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) will raise gasoline prices by 2.0 drachmas per litre, effective on Thursday.</p>
<p>Transport diesel and heating oil prices will go up by 1.9 and 1.8 drachmas per litre respectively, DEP said.</p>
<p>The price adjustments come after higher world gasoline prices, up by $5.2 per metric tonne, higher transport diesel prices, up by $4.3 per metric tonne, higher heating oil prices, up by $3.9 per metric tonne, and a firmer dollar/drachma, up 3.90 drachmas, it said.</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
